00:13:36.140 --> 00:13:39.900
Wow, there's so many!

00:13:39.900 --> 00:13:42.980
Th-The char I had so much trouble with...

00:13:42.980 --> 00:13:47.200
Well, that's a fishing hole.
Wanna fish here?

00:13:47.200 --> 00:13:49.280
I'm going to fish in the river! Harumph!

00:13:49.280 --> 00:13:51.450
R-Right...

00:13:54.580 --> 00:13:56.500
I wonder what I should use...

00:13:56.500 --> 00:14:01.630
Oh, yeah. I guess I should try this
if we can use salmon roe.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:03.550
Fly fishing with an egg-shaped fly!

00:14:03.550 --> 00:14:06.010
You can catch plenty
with this egg-shaped fly,

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:08.220
so I highly recommend them for beginners!

00:14:08.220 --> 00:14:10.010
This is an indicator.

00:14:10.010 --> 00:14:13.930
It's basically the same thing as
a floater and helps you catch fish!

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:16.350
Hm... It's a pain to put them on
and take them off, so never mind.

00:14:16.350 --> 00:14:20.190
The water's clear,
so I'll know when I get a bite.

00:14:29.910 --> 00:14:31.830
Here we go.

00:14:34.330 --> 00:14:36.450
I immediately got a bite.

00:14:36.450 --> 00:14:41.330
This might be easier than I thought,
so maybe I'll try other flies.

00:14:41.330 --> 00:14:46.090
If Koharu is having trouble,
I'll give her one of these.

00:14:47.220 --> 00:14:49.720
Today is the worst...

00:14:49.720 --> 00:14:51.430
I haven't caught any.

00:14:51.430 --> 00:14:54.720
The people at the campsite just
released some fish into the water, too.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:15:00.730
But I don't see any fish at all.
Hiyori always sees them so quickly.

00:15:00.730 --> 00:15:04.980
I know. I could've sworn
that a while back, Hiyori...

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:08.320
See that spot where
the water's pouring out?

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:13.450
Fish love spots like that,
so try aiming over there.

00:15:14.620 --> 00:15:16.240
Okay...

00:15:18.620 --> 00:15:22.750
I can't tell if there're any fish
because of the foam, but...

00:15:22.750 --> 00:15:25.420
Hiyah! Go for it!

00:15:28.630 --> 00:15:30.550
There!

00:15:33.350 --> 00:15:36.260
Rainbow trout!

00:15:36.260 --> 00:15:40.310
I actually looked for a place fish
might be myself and caught one!

00:15:41.770 --> 00:15:44.310
Right now...

00:15:44.310 --> 00:15:48.030
I feel like an actual fishing pro!

00:15:49.530 --> 00:15:51.780
Ah, Koharu...

00:15:51.780 --> 00:15:55.370
I got another one!
Yay! This is so much fun!

00:15:55.370 --> 00:15:57.990
Today's the best! Yay!

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:03.880
I caught so much,
so I'll try to find another spot!

00:16:03.880 --> 00:16:06.250
Hm... There aren't any fish.

00:16:06.250 --> 00:16:08.710
This seems hard.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:11.470
Hello, anything biting?

00:16:11.470 --> 00:16:13.510
That sounded like a real fishing question!

00:16:13.510 --> 00:16:16.600
U-Um, I think you might
have more luck if you go over to

00:16:16.600 --> 00:16:20.600
where it looks white from
the river hits those rocks.

00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:21.480
Huh...

00:16:21.480 --> 00:16:22.810
Oh, I see.

00:16:22.810 --> 00:16:24.440
Thank you very much!

00:16:24.440 --> 00:16:26.360
N-No problem.

00:16:26.360 --> 00:16:27.770
Hey, is that it?

00:16:27.770 --> 00:16:29.070
I think it's there.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:29.940
"Feeling Accomplished!!"

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:29.940
I think it's there.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:31.570
"Feeling Accomplished!!"

00:16:31.570 --> 00:16:35.700
Why do you look so pleased with yourself?

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:38.660
Koi! You're late!

00:16:38.660 --> 00:16:40.330
Oh? Looks like you caught a lot.

00:16:40.330 --> 00:16:44.420
Looks like we have plenty
for dinner with me catching any.

00:16:44.420 --> 00:16:47.710
You don't really like fishing, Koi?

00:16:47.710 --> 00:16:50.800
Well, not exactly.

00:16:50.800 --> 00:16:52.800
I think it's more...

00:16:52.800 --> 00:16:56.390
I like people who fish.

00:16:56.390 --> 00:16:58.640
I got one!

00:16:59.680 --> 00:17:01.180
--Even adults and even people
who don't talk much...

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:02.930
--Dang it! You beat me to it!
--Even adults and even people
who don't talk much,

00:17:02.930 --> 00:17:07.900
get this sparkly look on their face like
they're little kids when they're fishing.

00:17:07.900 --> 00:17:11.820
I think I like seeing that.

00:17:11.820 --> 00:17:17.780
Huh... Well in that case,
watch me to your heart's content!

00:17:17.780 --> 00:17:19.530
I am open for observation!

00:17:19.530 --> 00:17:21.410
Nah.

00:17:21.410 --> 00:17:26.420
But it's also different when it comes to
people who are as obsessed as my dad.

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:28.290
Oh...

00:17:28.290 --> 00:17:32.090
I know. Let's have them salt-grill
a few of them at the rest area.

00:17:32.090 --> 00:17:33.970
Good idea!

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.390
Let's eat!

00:17:41.140 --> 00:17:43.140
So good!

00:17:44.480 --> 00:17:48.900
Nothing beats salt-grilled river fish.

00:17:48.900 --> 00:17:51.690
That's not true!

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:55.740
I'm going to show you just how much I
learned in my river-fish cuisine research!

00:17:56.780 --> 00:17:59.620
Koharu's Kitchen!

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:01.660
Half an onion?

00:18:01.660 --> 00:18:03.290
Now what?

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.410
Slice and slice!

00:18:05.410 --> 00:18:07.620
Apply butter to some aluminum foil

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:11.040
and add your thinly-sliced onions
and <i>bunashimeji </i>mushrooms.

00:18:11.040 --> 00:18:14.340
Salt your rainbow trout and
leave it for about 20 minutes.

00:18:14.340 --> 00:18:17.840
Then wipe up any
moisture with a paper towel.

00:18:17.840 --> 00:18:22.470
Apply a mixture of miso and
mayonnaise onto your rainbow trout...

00:18:22.470 --> 00:18:25.640
And then wrap it up in the aluminum foil.

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:29.270
Line them up in the
frying pan and put on the lid.

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:33.820
Steam them on low heat
for 15 minutes.

00:18:33.820 --> 00:18:36.150
Huh...

00:18:36.150 --> 00:18:38.530
I think that should about do it.

00:18:40.240 --> 00:18:44.450
Rainbow trout cooked in foil
with mayo complete!

00:18:44.450 --> 00:18:48.250
I also made some with curry mayo
along with the miso mayo!

00:18:48.250 --> 00:18:50.080
Dig in!

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.050
Sho good!

00:18:56.050 --> 00:18:58.050
You bet it is.

00:18:58.050 --> 00:19:01.550
This is so good, Koharu!

00:19:05.850 --> 00:19:09.980
I can't, I'm so tired. Goodnight.

00:19:09.980 --> 00:19:11.650
Koharu, we're going to bed.

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.570
Aw...

00:19:19.320 --> 00:19:24.700
I can't... Today was so
much fun that I can't sleep!

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.790
Koi.

00:19:25.790 --> 00:19:26.870
Wh-What?

00:19:26.870 --> 00:19:28.750
Talk to me.

00:19:28.750 --> 00:19:30.710
Huh? About what?

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:33.630
Maybe about relationships
or like a scary story.

00:19:33.630 --> 00:19:35.250
Well...

00:19:35.250 --> 00:19:39.130
This is something I heard from my dad...

00:19:39.130 --> 00:19:41.260
Ooh, a scary story.

00:19:42.550 --> 00:19:46.770
When my dad and Yamahi's dad
were still students,

00:19:46.770 --> 00:19:49.730
they went to Hokkaido
for a fishing and camping trip.

00:19:49.730 --> 00:19:53.810
After fishing during the day,
they went back to their tent,

00:19:53.810 --> 00:19:57.900
it looked like a bear might've been by.

00:19:57.900 --> 00:20:00.740
But it was already late
and it was getting dark,

00:20:00.740 --> 00:20:06.160
so they decided to go to bed early
and get up early to go somewhere else...

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:12.460
The next day when they
woke up early in the morning...

00:20:18.050 --> 00:20:24.180
They both ran as fast as they could,
and they made the right choice.

00:20:24.180 --> 00:20:29.930
Brown bears become pretty obsessed
with prey they've almost caught,

00:20:29.930 --> 00:20:36.400
so they don't give up
and keep coming after you.

00:20:36.400 --> 00:20:38.480
That's way too scary!

00:20:38.480 --> 00:20:40.900
Wait, bears don't appear
around here, do they?

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:43.610
I mean, they look like they'd
come out here but they don't, right?

00:20:43.610 --> 00:20:45.490
I'm beat. I'm going to sleep.

00:20:45.490 --> 00:20:50.790
Hey, hello? Don't fall asleep, Koi!
Don't leave me alone!

00:20:54.120 --> 00:20:58.380
The wind is making the
trees make scary sounds...

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:01.050
What was that?!

00:21:03.930 --> 00:21:10.220
The sound of the river is scary...
I can't sleep.

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:18.480
--Bear... Bear...

00:21:18.480 --> 00:21:21.990
--What in the world happened?
--Bear... Bear...

00:21:21.990 --> 00:21:23.490
Mornin'.

00:21:23.490 --> 00:21:25.530
Morning, Hiyori.

00:21:25.530 --> 00:21:28.990
Good morning, you two! Breakfast is ready.

00:21:28.990 --> 00:21:34.330
Wow, you made this all by yourself?
That's amazing!

00:21:34.330 --> 00:21:37.380
Aha, so this is the famous char soup.

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:38.960
It smells so good!

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:41.420
Miso soup you have outdoors is the best!

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:43.340
I brought some pickled veggies. Want some?

00:21:43.340 --> 00:21:45.550
Yeah!

00:21:45.550 --> 00:21:50.220
Once we check out, we're going to
stop by the hot springs that're nearby.

00:21:50.220 --> 00:21:52.430
H-Hot springs?

00:23:23.690 --> 00:23:26.530
We haven't been in the
bath together for a while.

00:23:26.530 --> 00:23:28.700
Even though we used to bathe
together in grade school all the time.

00:23:28.700 --> 00:23:30.410
Yeah.

00:23:35.660 --> 00:23:38.330
What's wrong, Koharu?
We're going to go without you.

00:23:38.330 --> 00:23:40.250
You...

00:23:40.250 --> 00:23:43.460
You two are way too
comfortable with each other!

00:23:45.800 --> 00:23:49.010
You know, this was
a pretty satisfying trip.

00:23:49.010 --> 00:23:54.260
Yeah. I'd love to have
another trip like this with just us.

00:23:55.010 --> 00:23:55.680
"Next Time"

00:23:55.680 --> 00:23:58.680
"Next Time"
Hiyori, why do you have bells
on your backpack?

00:23:58.680 --> 00:23:59.600
"Next Time"
It's to keep bears away.

00:23:59.600 --> 00:24:00.440
"Next Time"
Bears?!

00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:02.980
"Next Time"
Don't forget your bells when
you go fishing in the mountains.

00:24:02.980 --> 00:24:05.650
"Next Time"
Okay! I'll put on lots!

00:24:05.650 --> 00:24:06.820
"Next Time"
Jingle, jingle, jingle, jingle!

00:24:06.820 --> 00:24:07.940
"Next Time"
Jingle, jingle, jingle, jingle!

00:24:07.940 --> 00:24:08.320
"Next Time"
--Jingle, jingle, jingle, jingle!

00:24:08.320 --> 00:24:09.940
"Next Time"
--Jingle, jingle, jingle, jingle!
--So noisy...
